  {
   "id": "6nr5Vu0gWmsJ",
   "from": "Heike Hofmann",
   "author": "20a8e3faa83e8923",
   "date": "2010-09-21T00:47:11Z",
   "subject": "Re: borders, mapproj, and plotting over 180 longitude",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\">Rob,<div><br></div><div>What you could do to get around the problem with the 180 degrees, is to subtract 360 from all the positive longitudinal values (in case you&#39;re just covering the Pacific, that should get rid of the arbitrary cutoff, since  -180 = +180)</div><div><br></div><div>Then your first strategy would do:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica;color:rgb(0,10,161)\"><span style=\"color:#000000\">xrng</span> &lt;- <span style=\"color:#000000\">c</span>(-<span style=\"color:#0f530d\">185</span>,-<span style=\"color:#0f530d\">110</span>)</div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica\">idx<span style=\"color:#000aa1\"> &lt;- </span>which<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">(</span>test<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">$</span>ssm_lon<span style=\"color:#000aa1\"> &gt; </span><span style=\"color:#0f530d\">0</span><span style=\"color:#000aa1\">)</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica\">test<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">$</span>ssm_lon<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">[</span>idx<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">] &lt;- </span>test<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">$</span>ssm_lon<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">[</span>idx<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">]-</span><span style=\"color:#0f530d\">360</span></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica;color:rgb(0,10,161);min-height:14px\"><br></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica\">m<span style=\"color:#000aa1\"> &lt;- </span>ggplot<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">(</span>data<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">=</span>test<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">, </span>aes<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">(</span>ssm_lon<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">, </span>ssm_lat<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">,</span>group<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">=</span>seal<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">))+</span></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000aa1\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span></span>geom_path<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">(</span>aes<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">(</span>colour<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">=</span>factor<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">(</span>seal<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">)))+</span></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000aa1\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span></span>borders<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">(</span><span style=\"color:#ad0900\">&#39;world&#39;</span><span style=\"color:#000aa1\">)+</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica\"><span style=\"color:#000aa1\"><span style=\"white-space:pre\">\t</span></span>coord_cartesian<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">(</span>xlim<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">=</span>xrng<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">, </span>ylim<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">=</span>yrng<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">)</span></div><div style=\"margin-top:0px;margin-right:0px;margin-bottom:0px;margin-left:0px;font:normal normal normal 12px/normal Helvetica\">print<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">(</span>m<span style=\"color:#000aa1\">)</span></div><div><font color=\"#000AA1\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000AA1\"><br></font></div></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div style=\"word-wrap:break-word\"><div><div><font color=\"#000AA1\">Heike</font></div><div><font color=\"#000AA1\"><br></font></div><div><font color=\"#000AA1\"></font></div></div></div>"
